# Styled runs, [text]{name} (reference/common/text-formatting.md): page of 240 × 160 with margins of 20, page area of
# 200 × 120 from (20, 20). Size 10 with Line height 15; with the test metrics each character measures 5 pt (a small
# cap, 4). The styles of the runs do not change the height of the lines: each text has the lines it would have without
# them, except the last, whose letter spacing makes it break. The image shows the colors, the fonts and the case.
#   colors: a price in red and bold, and a link whose text is a styled run. One line, y = 20.
#   fonts:  a run in IBM Plex Serif italic, one of weight 300 and one with inline code in the Code font of its style,
#           which the box does not have. y = 35.
#   caps:   small caps and upper case in two runs of a text that has neither. y = 50.
#   plain:  "Las letras espaciadas van", 25 characters, 125 in a box of 130: one line. y = 65.
#   spaced: the same text with "letras espaciadas" in upper case and with Letter spacing 2, also on its space:
#           15 + 5 + 17 × 7 + 5 + 15 = 159 does not fit. "Las LETRAS" measures 15 + 5 + 6 × 7, less the spacing of its
#           last letter, 60; "ESPACIADAS van", 10 × 7 + 5 + 15 = 90, whose last letter has none. y = 80, two lines.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 240
		Height: 160
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Line height: 15
				Markup: markdown
		For style: price
			Typography:
				Color: #B3261E
				Bold: true
		For style: serif
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Italic: true
		For style: light
			Typography:
				Weight: 300
		For style: code
			Typography:
				Code font: IBM Plex Mono
				Color: #12315A
		For style: caps
			Typography:
				Small caps: true
		For style: upper
			Typography:
				Case: uppercase
		For style: wide
			Typography:
				Letter spacing: 2
				Case: uppercase
		For style: narrow
			Box:
				Width: 130
	Section:
		Text: Total: [12,50 €]{price}, [[ver precio]{price}](https://example.com).
			Id: colors
		Text: En [serifa cursiva]{serif}, [ligera]{light} y [con `mono`]{code}.
			Id: fonts
		Text: Un [aviso]{caps} y [otro]{upper} más.
			Id: caps
		Text: Las letras espaciadas van
			Id: plain
			Style: narrow
		Text: Las [letras espaciadas]{wide} van
			Id: spaced
			Style: narrow
